Error [E0149]: a runtime `String` can't be used as `Sh`
  --> tests/ui/typed_text_process_run_string.jet:5:17
    |
  5 |     process.run("printf injected") ?? return
    |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a runtime string could change the executable or argument boundaries; only a checked literal may build `Sh`, where every `{value}` hole is exactly one argv item
 Fix: write `Sh.{"..."}` with `{value}` holes, or use `Sh.raw("…")` if you have audited the text
